      "receiptSource": "Original Receipt in \u0027\u003Ci\u003EThe Cook and Housekeeper\u0027s Dictionary\u003C/i\u003E\u0027 by Mary Eaton (\u003Ca href=\u0022references.html#eaton-1822\u0022\u003E\u003Cb\u003EEaton 1822\u003C/b\u003E\u003C/a\u003E);",
      "receiptText": "STAFFORDSHIRE BEEF STEAKS. Beat them a little with a rollingpin, then flour and season, and fry them of a fine light brown, with sliced onions. Lay the steaks into a stewpan, and pour over them as much boiling water as will serve for sauce. Stew them very gently for half an hour, and add a spoonful of ketchup or walnut liquor, before they are served up.\u003Cbr\u003E"
    }
